- BUG if expecting expression but got eof will make the compiler get stuck
    even doing checks for eof seems to not work unless the file ended with a line feed

- arrays:
    - slices
    - iterators
    - implement inner and outer mutability such as 'const ^i32' and '^const i32' should be different and a combination of both should be possible.
    - currently deeply nested types can be parsed but the type information is lost and not used. such as '^^i32'.
    - allow setting the size of a static array with any compile time constant not just integer literals.
    - convert string to be '[]const char' slice
    - enum indexed arrays
    - type cache

- structs:
    - var user3: User = {name: "jack", score: 10}
    - during struct initialization any unspecified field should be set to its default value.
    - anonymous nested structs
    - structural struct equality. eg: fn take_structure(s: {x: i32, s: str}). then can pass any struct that even partially matches this structure
    - reflection
    - refactor attributes to allow user defined types
    - name mangling
    - methods
    - null coalescing
    - traits
    - readonly attribute
    - offsetof operator for struct fields
    - raii
    - operator overloading
    - mixins
    - move and copy system
    - allow initialization of structs without braces (maybe bad idea?)

- other core features:
    - enums
    - generics
    - context system
    - errors

- non-core features:
    - defer
    - union literals A | B
    - unions
    - error unions
    - pattern matching
    - comptime blocks
    - closures
    - tuples and destructuring
    - string interpolation

